#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""dreamteam — io-shield: make I/O weights real on this host, give the known hogs a low one, and give the fleet
lead's own scope the kernel OOM score a user cannot give itself.

A SYSTEM tool (root). The copy of record is here; the installed copy is /usr/local/sbin/dreamteam-io-shield, put
there by scripts/host/io-shield-install and by nothing else (systemd/system/README.md).

WHY (Flow rows 7e039111, f72945bc; measured 2026-11-21/23).
  1. An interactive session froze while "idle class, nice 15" jobs ran. The reader was not the job: a palace test
     asks Postgres, and Postgres (its own cgroup, normal class) read 60 MB/s for one SELECT. A client's nice level
     stops at the socket.
  2. No weight was in force anywhere: a cgroup's IOWeight= does nothing until io.cost is enabled for the device,
     and the default io.cost settings barely help. On an NVMe, a victim against 4 readers and 1 writer:
         alone                                   fsync p99   4.5 ms
         hogs, no control                        fsync p99 453   ms
         io.cost with latency targets, 10 : 100  fsync p99   7.7 ms   (hogs still 267 MB/s read)
  3. A user process cannot lower its own oom_score_adj. Root can.

USAGE   io-shield [--throwaway] apply|off|on|status
CONFIG  /etc/dreamteam/io-shield.conf (host data, never in this repo), one line each:
  device <name> [rlat=<µs>] [wlat=<µs>] [min=<pct>] [max=<pct>]    io.cost on /sys/block/<name>, latency targets
  unit <name>.service <weight>        IOWeight (1-10000) on that SERVICE, at runtime only. Only *.service is
                                      accepted: a slice, a scope (a lane's, the lead's) and user@<uid>.service are
                                      refused by the shape of the name, before anything is done.
  docker <container> <weight>         the same for that container's scope, docker-<full id>.scope
  oomprotect <uid> lead-<name>.scope <score>     every process of <uid> in EXACTLY
        <cgroup root>/user.slice/user-<uid>.slice/user@<uid>.service/app.slice/lead-<name>.scope  (and below)
        whose score is not already negative gets <score> (-1000..0). No mark, attribute, other unit name or
        parent slice earns it.
  Any other line, or a bad value, stops the run before anything is written (exit 22).

THE LEDGER (default /run/dreamteam-io-shield, root only, 0700, gone at reboot like everything it speaks of).
EVERYTHING this tool changes is recorded there FIRST, durably (written whole, fsync, rename, fsync of the
directory), and `off` undoes ONLY what is recorded:
  <pid>               start=<starttime> unit=<lead unit> score=<n> prev=<n> uid=<n>      an OOM score we wrote
  unit.<unit name>    ours=<weight> prev=<weight or unset>                                an IOWeight we set
  dev.<maj>_<min>     prev=<the device's io.cost.qos line before us, or none>             io.cost we enabled
  left/<pid>.<start>  a score record RETIRED: its process left its lead unit holding our score (see below)
A unit or device named in the config that has no record is NOT touched by `off` (an `off` without an `apply`
writes nothing but the stamp). A previous non-default weight or qos line is put back, not discarded.
FAIL CLOSED. The ledger is read whole and strictly before ANY change: an entry that is not a regular file of
ours, not one canonical newline-terminated line, or of an unknown name stops the run (exit 1) with nothing
written anywhere. So does a ledger directory that is a symlink, not ours, or writable by others. So does any
read, write or delete that fails with anything but "it is gone" (EACCES, EIO, ...): the record is kept, the run
stops before the next change. Only ENOENT / ESRCH mean a process has ended.

THE UNDO OF A SCORE IS NARROWER THAN THE WRITE. A score is written back in one case only: `off`, the same process
(pid and start time), still holding the score we wrote, its cgroup STILL the lead unit of its record. A recorded
process found anywhere else is not written, under /system.slice first of all: its record is retired to left/ and
`status` names it. A negative score this tool has no record of is never written to, wherever the process lives.
  The placement is read again immediately before every write, through the same /proc/<pid> descriptor, and once
  more after a new score: a process that left meanwhile has its fresh record retired at once. WHAT THAT IS NOT:
  an atomic check-and-write. The kernel has none; a process moved by its owner between the last read and the
  write (two system calls) is written once. It then shows as "left" and is never written again. Closing that
  window needs lanes under their own uid, not a check here; the same goes for a same-uid process that puts
  itself into the lead's cgroup.

ONE LOCK (/run/dreamteam-io-shield.lock) for apply, off and on, the timer's run and a run by hand alike; a run
that cannot have it in time does nothing (exit 75). status takes none.

ROOT RUNS ARE NOT STEERABLE. As root every path above is fixed, PATH is /usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin and every
IO_SHIELD_* variable is ignored. The seams exist only for a caller that is NOT root (the tests), which can reach
nothing that needs root.

FIRST USE IS A THROWAWAY UNIT, BY CONSTRUCTION. Production `apply` refuses (exit 3) unless
/var/lib/dreamteam/io-shield.accepted exists, is root's, and holds the sha256 of THIS file. Only
`io-shield-accept <uid> throwaway` writes it, after a full apply-and-off on a throwaway lead unit with every
named service untouched. `--throwaway` reads /etc/dreamteam/io-shield-throwaway.conf, which may hold nothing but
`oomprotect <uid> lead-throwaway-<name>.scope <score>` lines, and keeps its own ledger, lock and stamp
(/run/dreamteam-io-shield-throwaway*). A production config may not name a lead-throwaway-* unit.

Exit: 0 done · 1 something failed or could not be trusted (nothing further was changed) · 2 not root, or no
config · 3 not accepted on this host yet · 22 bad argument or config line · 75 the lock stayed held.
"""
import errno
import fcntl
import hashlib
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time

ME = "io-shield"
GONE = (errno.ENOENT, errno.ESRCH, errno.ENOTDIR)
LEADRE = re.compile(r"^lead-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,80}\.scope$")
THROWRE = re.compile(r"^lead-throwaway-[a-z0-9]{1,40}\.scope$")
SERVICERE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9@_.:-]{0,200}\.service$")
DOCKERRE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,200}$")
DOCKUNIT = re.compile(r"^docker-[0-9a-f]{64}\.scope$")
SCORE_LINE = re.compile(r"^start=([0-9]{1,20}) unit=(lead-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,80}\.scope) score=(0|-[0-9]{1,4}) prev=(-?[0-9]{1,4}) uid=([0-9]{1,9})\n$")
UNIT_LINE = re.compile(r"^ours=([0-9]{1,5}) prev=([0-9]{1,5}|unset)\n$")
DEV_LINE = re.compile(r"^prev=(none|[0-9]+:[0-9]+ [ -~]{1,300})\n$")


class Stop(Exception):
    """Something failed or could not be trusted: say it, change nothing further, exit 1."""


def err(msg):
    sys.stderr.write("%s: %s\n" % (ME, msg))


def die(code, msg):
    err(msg)
    sys.exit(code)


# ── where things are. As root: fixed. Not root (tests): the seams.
ARGS = sys.argv[1:]
THROW = bool(ARGS) and ARGS[0] == "--throwaway"
if THROW:
    ARGS = ARGS[1:]
if len(ARGS) != 1 or ARGS[0] not in ("apply", "off", "on", "status"):
    die(22, "usage: io-shield [--throwaway] apply|off|on|status")
MODE = ARGS[0]
ROOT = os.geteuid() == 0
if ROOT:
    E = {}
    os.environ.clear()
    os.environ.update({"PATH": "/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin", "LANG": "C"})
else:
    E = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k.startswith("IO_SHIELD_")}
SUF = "-throwaway" if THROW else ""
RUN = E.get("IO_SHIELD_RUN_DIR", "/run")
CONF = E.get("IO_SHIELD_THROWAWAY_CONF" if THROW else "IO_SHIELD_CONF", "/etc/dreamteam/io-shield%s.conf" % SUF)
QOS = E.get("IO_SHIELD_QOS_FILE", "/sys/fs/cgroup/io.cost.qos")
SYSBLOCK = E.get("IO_SHIELD_SYSBLOCK", "/sys/block")
CGROOT = E.get("IO_SHIELD_CGROUP_ROOT", "/sys/fs/cgroup")
PROC = E.get("IO_SHIELD_PROC", "/proc")
LEDGER = E.get("IO_SHIELD_LEDGER", RUN + "/dreamteam-io-shield") + SUF
STAMP = RUN + "/dreamteam-io-shield%s.off" % SUF
LOCKF = RUN + "/dreamteam-io-shield%s.lock" % SUF
ACCEPTED = E.get("IO_SHIELD_ACCEPTED", "/var/lib/dreamteam/io-shield.accepted")
LEFT = os.path.join(LEDGER, "left")
try:
    LOCKWAIT = int(E.get("IO_SHIELD_LOCK_WAIT", "60"))
    if not 0 <= LOCKWAIT <= 999:
        LOCKWAIT = 60
except ValueError:
    LOCKWAIT = 60

if not (os.path.isfile(CONF) and os.access(CONF, os.R_OK)):
    die(2, "no readable config at %s" % CONF)
if MODE != "status" and not ROOT and E.get("IO_SHIELD_ASSUME_ROOT") != "1":
    die(2, "%s needs root" % MODE)


# ── the config: read whole, refused whole
def bad(n, msg):
    die(22, "%s line %d: %s" % (CONF, n, msg))


DEVS, UNITS, DOCK, OOM = [], [], [], []
for n, line in enumerate(open(CONF, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace").read().split("\n"), 1):
    w = line.split()
    if not w or w[0].startswith("#"):
        continue
    if THROW and w[0] != "oomprotect":
        bad(n, "a throwaway config holds only oomprotect lines (got '%s')" % w[0])
    if w[0] == "device":
        if len(w) < 2 or not re.match(r"^[a-z0-9]{1,32}$", w[1]):
            bad(n, "device needs a plain block device name")
        v = {"rlat": 2000, "wlat": 5000, "min": 25, "max": 100}
        for kv in w[2:]:
            k, _, x = kv.partition("=")
            if not re.match(r"^[0-9]{1,7}$", x):
                bad(n, "'%s' is not key=<number>" % kv)
            if k not in v:
                bad(n, "unknown key '%s' (rlat wlat min max)" % k)
            v[k] = int(x)
        if not (1 <= v["min"] <= v["max"] <= 10000 and v["rlat"] >= 1 and v["wlat"] >= 1):
            bad(n, "need 1 <= min <= max <= 10000 and latencies of at least 1 µs")
        DEVS.append((w[1], "ctrl=user rpct=95.00 rlat=%d wpct=95.00 wlat=%d min=%d.00 max=%d.00" % (v["rlat"], v["wlat"], v["min"], v["max"])))
    elif w[0] in ("unit", "docker"):
        if len(w) != 3 or not re.match(r"^[0-9]{1,7}$", w[2]) or not 1 <= int(w[2]) <= 10000:
            bad(n, "%s needs <name> <weight 1-10000>" % w[0])
        if w[0] == "unit":
            # BY THE SHAPE OF THE NAME: a service, and never the user manager itself. system.slice, any other slice,
            # lead-<x>.scope and a lane's scope cannot be written as a *.service name.
            if not SERVICERE.match(w[1]) or re.match(r"^user@", w[1]) or w[1].startswith("systemd-"):
                bad(n, "'%s' is not a service this tool may weight (a plain <name>.service; never a slice, a scope, user@<uid>.service or systemd-*)" % w[1])
            UNITS.append((w[1], w[2]))
        else:
            if not DOCKERRE.match(w[1]):
                bad(n, "'%s' is not a plain name" % w[1])
            DOCK.append((w[1], w[2]))
    elif w[0] == "oomprotect":
        ok = len(w) == 4 and re.match(r"^[0-9]{1,9}$", w[1]) and LEADRE.match(w[2]) and re.match(r"^(0|-[0-9]{1,4})$", w[3]) and int(w[3]) >= -1000
        if not ok:
            bad(n, "oomprotect needs <uid> <lead-NAME.scope> <score -1000..0>")
        if THROW and not THROWRE.match(w[2]):
            bad(n, "a throwaway config names only lead-throwaway-<name>.scope units (got '%s')" % w[2])
        if not THROW and w[2].startswith("lead-throwaway-"):
            bad(n, "'%s' is a throwaway unit name: it belongs in the throwaway config, never here" % w[2])
        OOM.append((w[1], w[2], w[3]))
    else:
        bad(n, "unknown word '%s' (device, unit, docker, oomprotect)" % w[0])


# ── commands
def run(*cmd):
    """(exit status, stdout). The command is found through PATH: fixed for root, the caller's otherwise."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(cmd, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, text=True, pass_fds=())
        return r.returncode, r.stdout
    except OSError:
        return 127, ""


def devno(name):
    try:
        d = open(os.path.join(SYSBLOCK, name, "dev")).read().strip()
    except OSError:
        return None
    return d if re.match(r"^[0-9]+:[0-9]+$", d) else None


def docker_unit(name):
    rc, out = run("docker", "inspect", "-f", "{{.Id}}", name)
    out = out.strip()
    return "docker-%s.scope" % out if rc == 0 and re.match(r"^[0-9a-f]{64}$", out) else None


def unit_state(unit):
    """(LoadState, IOWeight) from ONE systemctl call. A call that fails is not "not loaded": it stops the run."""
    rc, out = run("systemctl", "show", unit, "-p", "LoadState", "-p", "IOWeight")
    kv = dict(l.split("=", 1) for l in out.split("\n") if "=" in l)
    if rc != 0 or "LoadState" not in kv:
        raise Stop("systemctl show %s failed (exit %d): its state is unknown, nothing set on it" % (unit, rc))
    return kv["LoadState"], kv.get("IOWeight", "")


# ── the ledger
def wr_durable(path, text):
    """The whole text, on disk, under its final name, or an exception: never a partial file under that name."""
    d = os.path.dirname(path)
    tmp = os.path.join(d, ".%s.tmp" % os.path.basename(path))
    try:
        os.unlink(tmp)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    data = text.encode()
    fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)
    try:
        done = 0
        while done < len(data):
            done += os.write(fd, data[done:])
        os.fsync(fd)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    os.replace(tmp, path)
    dfd = os.open(d, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY)
    try:
        os.fsync(dfd)
    finally:
        os.close(dfd)


def rm_record(path):
    """Gone already is fine. Any other failure stops the run: a record we cannot remove is a record we still hold."""
    try:
        os.unlink(path)
    except OSError as e:
        if e.errno not in GONE:
            raise Stop("cannot remove the record %s (%s): stopping" % (path, e.strerror))


def ledger_dir(create):
    """True when there is a ledger of ours to read; False when there is none (and none was asked for).
    A ledger that is there and cannot be trusted stops the run."""
    if os.path.islink(LEDGER):
        raise Stop("the ledger %s is a symlink: not trusted, nothing done" % LEDGER)
    if not os.path.lexists(LEDGER):
        if not create:
            return False
        os.makedirs(LEDGER, mode=0o700)
    st = os.lstat(LEDGER)
    if not os.path.isdir(LEDGER) or st.st_uid != os.geteuid() or st.st_mode & 0o022:
        raise Stop("the ledger %s is not a directory of ours that only we can write: not trusted, nothing done" % LEDGER)
    return True


def load_ledger():
    """({pid: score record}, {unit: (ours, prev)}, {maj:min: prev line or None}). STRICT: every entry is one of the
    known names, a regular file of ours, one canonical line; anything else stops the run."""
    scores, units, devs = {}, {}, {}
    for n in sorted(os.listdir(LEDGER)):
        p = os.path.join(LEDGER, n)
        if n == "left":
            if os.path.islink(p) or not os.path.isdir(p):
                raise Stop("%s is not a directory: the ledger is damaged, nothing done" % p)
            continue
        if n.startswith(".") and n.endswith(".tmp"):
            continue                                     # an interrupted publish: never renamed, so never a record
        st = os.lstat(p)
        if os.path.islink(p) or not os.path.isfile(p) or st.st_uid != os.geteuid():
            raise Stop("ledger entry %s is not a regular file of ours: the ledger is damaged, nothing done" % p)
        try:
            text = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as e:
            raise Stop("ledger entry %s cannot be read (%s): nothing done" % (p, e))
        if n.isdigit():
            m = SCORE_LINE.match(text)
            if m:
                scores[n] = {"start": m.group(1), "unit": m.group(2), "score": m.group(3), "prev": m.group(4), "uid": m.group(5)}
        elif n.startswith("unit."):
            m = UNIT_LINE.match(text) if (SERVICERE.match(n[5:]) or DOCKUNIT.match(n[5:])) else None
            if m:
                units[n[5:]] = (m.group(1), m.group(2))
        elif n.startswith("dev."):
            m = DEV_LINE.match(text) if re.match(r"^[0-9]+_[0-9]+$", n[4:]) else None
            if m:
                devs[n[4:].replace("_", ":")] = None if m.group(1) == "none" else m.group(1)
        else:
            m = None
        if not m:
            raise Stop("ledger entry %s is not a whole record of a known kind (half-written or foreign): the ledger is damaged, nothing done" % p)
    return scores, units, devs


# ── processes: one directory descriptor on /proc/<pid>; everything read and written goes through it
def rd(fd, name):
    f = os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY, dir_fd=fd)
    try:
        return os.read(f, 65536).decode("utf-8", "replace")
    finally:
        os.close(f)


def wr_score(fd, value):
    f = os.open("oom_score_adj", os.O_WRONLY | os.O_TRUNC, dir_fd=fd)
    try:
        os.write(f, (value + "\n").encode())
    finally:
        os.close(f)


def place(fd):
    return rd(fd, "cgroup").strip().split("\n")[-1].split("::", 1)[-1]


def hold(pid, uid):
    """(fd, starttime, cgroup, score) of a live process of <uid>; None when it is GONE or is another user's.
    Any other failure (EACCES, EIO, ...) is not absence: it raises Stop. The caller closes fd."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(os.path.join(PROC, pid), os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY)
    except OSError as e:
        if e.errno in GONE:
            return None
        raise Stop("cannot look at process %s (%s): it is not known to be gone, stopping" % (pid, e.strerror))
    try:
        if os.fstat(fd).st_uid != int(uid):
            os.close(fd)
            return None
        stat = rd(fd, "stat")
        return fd, stat[stat.rindex(")") + 2:].split()[19], place(fd), rd(fd, "oom_score_adj").strip()
    except OSError as e:
        os.close(fd)
        if e.errno in GONE:
            return None
        raise Stop("cannot read process %s (%s): it is not known to be gone, stopping" % (pid, e.strerror))
    except (ValueError, IndexError):
        os.close(fd)
        raise Stop("process %s: its stat line could not be parsed, stopping" % pid)


def unit_path(uid, unit):
    return "/user.slice/user-%s.slice/user@%s.service/app.slice/%s" % (uid, uid, unit)


def still_in(cg, uid, unit):
    """Is this cgroup the lead unit (or below it)? Never under /system.slice, never for a name that is not a lead
    unit name, never when that unit's directory is not a real directory."""
    if cg.startswith("/system.slice") or not LEADRE.match(unit or ""):
        return False
    r = unit_path(uid, unit)
    d = CGROOT + r
    return os.path.isdir(d) and not os.path.islink(d) and (cg == r or cg.startswith(r + "/"))


def retire(pid, r):
    """The record goes aside, durably, for a person; the process is not written."""
    if os.path.islink(LEFT):
        raise Stop("%s is a symlink: stopping" % LEFT)
    os.makedirs(LEFT, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    try:
        os.replace(os.path.join(LEDGER, pid), os.path.join(LEFT, "%s.%s" % (pid, r["start"])))
    except OSError as e:
        raise Stop("cannot retire the record of %s (%s): it is kept, stopping" % (pid, e.strerror))


def left_entries():
    try:
        return sorted(os.listdir(LEFT)) if os.path.isdir(LEFT) and not os.path.islink(LEFT) else []
    except OSError as e:
        raise Stop("cannot list %s (%s): stopping" % (LEFT, e.strerror))


def sweep_left():
    """Forget the retired records whose process has ended (pid AND start time)."""
    for n in left_entries():
        pid, _, start = n.partition(".")
        alive = False
        if pid.isdigit():
            try:
                stat = open(os.path.join(PROC, pid, "stat")).read()
                alive = stat[stat.rindex(")") + 2:].split()[19] == start
            except OSError as e:
                if e.errno not in GONE:
                    raise Stop("cannot read process %s (%s): its retired record is kept, stopping" % (pid, e.strerror))
            except (ValueError, IndexError):
                raise Stop("process %s: its stat line could not be parsed, stopping" % pid)
        if not alive:
            rm_record(os.path.join(LEFT, n))


def score_records(recs, reset, only=None):
    """The records. A write happens in exactly one case: reset, the same process, our score, STILL in its lead unit
    at the moment before the write. Returns (undone, retired)."""
    undone = retired = 0
    for pid, r in recs.items():
        if only and (r["uid"], r["unit"]) != only:
            continue
        h = hold(pid, r["uid"])
        if h is None:
            rm_record(os.path.join(LEDGER, pid))         # gone: nothing to undo, nobody written
            continue
        fd, start, cg, cur = h
        try:
            if start != r["start"] or cur != r["score"]:
                rm_record(os.path.join(LEDGER, pid))     # another process has that number now, or someone changed the score: not ours
            elif not still_in(cg, r["uid"], r["unit"]):
                retire(pid, r); retired += 1             # it left its lead unit holding our score: not written
            elif reset:
                if not still_in(place(fd), r["uid"], r["unit"]):       # read again, immediately before the write
                    retire(pid, r); retired += 1
                else:
                    wr_score(fd, r["prev"]); undone += 1
                    rm_record(os.path.join(LEDGER, pid))
        except OSError as e:
            if e.errno in GONE:
                rm_record(os.path.join(LEDGER, pid))
            else:
                raise Stop("undo for %s failed (%s): its record is kept, stopping" % (pid, e.strerror))
        finally:
            os.close(fd)
    return undone, retired


def score_unit(uid, unit, score, recs):
    """Score the processes in the lead unit: only a score that is not already negative, the record first.
    Returns (scored, left as found, retired)."""
    rel = unit_path(uid, unit)
    unit_dir = CGROOT + rel
    scored = asfound = retired = 0
    if not (os.path.isdir(unit_dir) and not os.path.islink(unit_dir)):
        return 0, 0, 0
    inside = lambda cg: cg == rel or cg.startswith(rel + "/")
    for sub, _, _ in os.walk(unit_dir):
        try:
            pids = open(os.path.join(sub, "cgroup.procs")).read().split()
        except OSError as e:
            if e.errno in GONE:
                continue
            raise Stop("cannot read %s/cgroup.procs (%s): stopping" % (sub, e.strerror))
        for pid in pids:
            h = hold(pid, uid) if pid.isdigit() else None
            if h is None:
                continue
            fd, start, cg, cur = h
            try:
                if not inside(cg):
                    continue                             # listed there a moment ago, not there now
                if pid in recs and recs[pid]["start"] == start:
                    continue                             # ours already
                if cur.startswith("-"):
                    asfound += 1
                    continue                             # a negative score we did not write: not ours to touch
                rec = {"start": start, "unit": unit, "score": score, "prev": cur, "uid": uid}
                path = os.path.join(LEDGER, pid)
                wr_durable(path, "start=%s unit=%s score=%s prev=%s uid=%s\n" % (start, unit, score, cur, uid))
                if not inside(place(fd)):                # read again, immediately before the write
                    rm_record(path)
                    continue
                try:
                    wr_score(fd, score)
                except OSError:
                    rm_record(path)                      # no score was written: no record of one may remain
                    raise
                scored += 1
                if not inside(place(fd)):                # it left while we wrote: it holds our score elsewhere now
                    retire(pid, rec); retired += 1; scored -= 1
            except OSError as e:
                if e.errno not in GONE:
                    raise Stop("score for %s failed (%s): stopping" % (pid, e.strerror))
            finally:
                os.close(fd)
    return scored, asfound, retired


def qos_lines():
    try:
        return [l for l in open(QOS).read().split("\n") if l.strip()]
    except OSError as e:
        raise Stop("cannot read %s (%s)" % (QOS, e.strerror))


def qos_write(line):
    with open(QOS, "w") as f:
        f.write(line + "\n")


def accepted():
    """The acceptance flag: root's, a regular file nobody else can write, holding the sha256 of THIS file."""
    try:
        st = os.lstat(ACCEPTED)                           # the entry itself: a symlink is never followed
        if (st.st_mode & 0o170000) != 0o100000 or st.st_uid != os.geteuid() or st.st_mode & 0o022:
            return False
        mine = hashlib.sha256(open(os.path.abspath(__file__), "rb").read()).hexdigest()
        return ("sha256=%s" % mine) in open(ACCEPTED).read().split("\n")
    except OSError:
        return False


# ── status: read-only, no lock, never changes the ledger
def status():
    try:
        print("io.cost.qos: %s" % ";".join(open(QOS).read().split("\n")))
    except OSError:
        print("io.cost.qos: ")
    if os.path.lexists(STAMP):
        print("OFF: %s exists, apply does nothing until 'io-shield on' or a reboot" % STAMP)
    if not THROW and not accepted():
        print("NOT ACCEPTED on this host: apply refuses until 'io-shield-accept <uid> throwaway' has passed for this helper (%s)" % ACCEPTED)
    scores, units, devs = {}, {}, {}
    trusted = True
    try:
        if ledger_dir(False):
            scores, units, devs = load_ledger()
    except (Stop, OSError) as e:
        trusted = False
        print("LEDGER NOT TRUSTED: %s" % e)
    for u, w in UNITS:
        rc, out = run("systemctl", "show", u, "-p", "IOWeight", "--value")
        print("unit %s: want %s, IOWeight=%s%s" % (u, w, out.strip(), " (recorded as ours)" if u in units else ""))
    for c, w in DOCK:
        u = docker_unit(c)
        if u:
            rc, out = run("systemctl", "show", u, "-p", "IOWeight", "--value")
            print("docker %s: want %s, %s IOWeight=%s%s" % (c, w, u, out.strip(), " (recorded as ours)" if u in units else ""))
        else:
            print("docker %s: want %s, not running" % (c, w))
    for uid, unit, score in OOM:
        ins, gone = [], []
        unit_dir = CGROOT + unit_path(uid, unit)
        try:
            if os.path.isdir(unit_dir) and not os.path.islink(unit_dir):
                for sub, _, _ in os.walk(unit_dir):
                    try:
                        pids = open(os.path.join(sub, "cgroup.procs")).read().split()
                    except OSError:
                        continue
                    for pid in pids:
                        h = hold(pid, uid) if pid.isdigit() else None
                        if h:
                            os.close(h[0])
                            ours = pid in scores and scores[pid]["start"] == h[1]
                            ins.append("%s=%s%s" % (pid, h[3], "" if ours else "(not ours)"))
            if trusted:
                for n in left_entries():
                    pid, _, start = n.partition(".")
                    h = hold(pid, uid) if pid.isdigit() else None
                    if h:
                        if h[1] == start:
                            gone.append("%s=%s(%s)" % (pid, h[3], h[2].rstrip("/").split("/")[-1] or "/"))
                        os.close(h[0])
        except Stop as e:
            print("oomprotect uid %s unit %s: want %s; COULD NOT BE READ: %s" % (uid, unit, score, e))
            continue
        print("oomprotect uid %s unit %s: want %s; in:%s; recorded:%s; left the unit holding our score, NOT written:%s" % (
            uid, unit, score, " ".join(ins) or "none", " ".join("%s(%s)" % (p, r["unit"]) for p, r in scores.items() if r["uid"] == uid) or "none", " ".join(gone) or "none"))
    return 0


# ── the verbs that change something: one lock, the ledger read whole first, stop at the first thing that fails
def changing():
    rc = 0
    if MODE == "on":
        try:
            os.unlink(STAMP)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass
        print("on: the stamp is gone; the next apply applies")
        return 0
    if MODE == "apply":
        if os.path.lexists(STAMP):
            print("off (%s exists): nothing applied" % STAMP)
            return 0
        if not THROW and not accepted():
            err("NOT ACCEPTED on this host: %s is missing, not root's, or not for this helper. Run 'io-shield-accept <uid> throwaway' first; nothing applied" % ACCEPTED)
            return 3
        ledger_dir(True)
    scores, units, devs = load_ledger() if ledger_dir(False) else ({}, {}, {})          # STRICT, before any change
    if MODE == "off":
        with open(STAMP, "w"):
            pass
        print("stamp written: %s (apply does nothing until 'io-shield on' or a reboot)" % STAMP)
        for mm, prev in devs.items():                    # ONLY what we recorded
            qos_write(prev if prev else "%s enable=0" % mm)
            rm_record(os.path.join(LEDGER, "dev.%s" % mm.replace(":", "_")))
            print("io.cost off on %s%s" % (mm, " (the line it had before us is back)" if prev else ""))
        for d, _ in DEVS:
            mm = devno(d)
            if mm and mm not in devs:
                print("note: io.cost on %s (%s) was not enabled by this tool (no record): not written" % (d, mm))
        for u, (ours, prev) in units.items():            # ONLY what we recorded
            state, cur = unit_state(u)
            if state == "loaded":
                if run("systemctl", "set-property", "--runtime", u, "IOWeight=")[0] != 0:
                    raise Stop("set-property failed for %s: its record is kept, stopping" % u)
                if prev != "unset" and unit_state(u)[1] != prev:
                    if run("systemctl", "set-property", "--runtime", u, "IOWeight=%s" % prev)[0] != 0:
                        raise Stop("could not put IOWeight=%s back on %s: its record is kept, stopping" % (prev, u))
                print("IOWeight=%s on %s (what it was before us)" % ("<default>" if prev == "unset" else prev, u))
            else:
                print("note: %s is not loaded now; its runtime setting went with it" % u)
            rm_record(os.path.join(LEDGER, "unit.%s" % u))
        named = [u for u, _ in UNITS] + [x for x in (docker_unit(c) for c, _ in DOCK) if x]
        for u in named:
            if u not in units:
                print("note: %s has no record of ours: not written" % u)
        for uid in sorted({r["uid"] for r in scores.values()} | {o[0] for o in OOM}):        # every record, whatever the config says now
            undone, retired = score_records({p: r for p, r in scores.items() if r["uid"] == uid}, True)
            print("oom scores of uid %s: %d of OUR recorded score(s), each still in its lead unit, put back to what they were; %d recorded process(es) had LEFT their unit holding our score and were NOT written (status names them); nothing else is touched" % (
                uid, undone, retired))
        if ledger_dir(False):
            sweep_left()
        return 0
    # apply
    have = {l.split()[0]: l for l in qos_lines()} if DEVS else {}
    for d, q in DEVS:
        mm = devno(d)
        if not mm:
            err("no device %s here" % d); rc = 1
            continue
        if mm not in devs:                               # the record FIRST: what the device had before us
            prev = have.get(mm)
            wr_durable(os.path.join(LEDGER, "dev.%s" % mm.replace(":", "_")), "prev=%s\n" % (prev if prev and "enable=1" in prev.split() else "none"))
            devs[mm] = prev
        qos_write("%s enable=1 %s" % (mm, q))
        print("io.cost on %s (%s): %s" % (d, mm, q))
    todo = [(u, w, u) for u, w in UNITS]
    for c, w in DOCK:
        u = docker_unit(c)
        if u:
            todo.append((u, w, "container %s" % c))
        else:
            print("note: container %s is not there now; the next run sets it" % c)
    for u, w, label in todo:
        state, cur = unit_state(u)
        if state != "loaded":
            print("note: %s is not loaded now; the next run sets it" % label)
            continue
        new = u not in units
        if new:                                          # the record FIRST: the weight it had before us
            wr_durable(os.path.join(LEDGER, "unit.%s" % u), "ours=%s prev=%s\n" % (w, cur if re.match(r"^[0-9]{1,5}$", cur) else "unset"))
        if run("systemctl", "set-property", "--runtime", u, "IOWeight=%s" % w)[0] != 0:
            if new:
                rm_record(os.path.join(LEDGER, "unit.%s" % u))       # nothing was set: no record of a setting may remain
            raise Stop("set-property failed for %s: stopping" % label)
        units[u] = (w, "unset")
        print("IOWeight=%s on %s" % (w, label))
    for uid, unit, score in OOM:
        _, retired = score_records(scores, False, (uid, unit))
        scores = load_ledger()[0]
        scored, asfound, ret2 = score_unit(uid, unit, score, scores)
        print("oomprotect uid %s unit %s: %d process(es) scored %s and recorded; %d in the unit left as found (a negative score we did not write); %d of ours have LEFT the unit holding our score and were NOT written (status names them)" % (
            uid, unit, scored, score, asfound, retired + ret2))
    sweep_left()
    return rc


def main():
    if MODE == "status":
        return status()
    try:
        lock = os.open(LOCKF, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_CLOEXEC, 0o600)        # CLOEXEC: nothing we start holds it
    except OSError as e:
        die(1, "cannot open the lock %s (%s)" % (LOCKF, e.strerror))
    end = time.monotonic() + LOCKWAIT
    while True:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            break
        except OSError:
            if time.monotonic() >= end:
                die(75, "another io-shield run holds %s (waited %d s): nothing done" % (LOCKF, LOCKWAIT))
            time.sleep(0.05)
    try:
        return changing()
    except Stop as e:
        err(str(e))
        return 1
    except OSError as e:
        err("%s: %s; stopped, nothing further changed" % (e.filename or "a write", e.strerror))
        return 1


sys.stdout.reconfigure(line_buffering=True)
sys.exit(main())
